### 0. Log In to Get JWT Token
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "joh@gmail.com",
    "password": "pass123"
}

### -----------------------------------------

@token = PASTE_YOUR_LONG_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Get All Courses (Public)
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/courses

### 2. Create a Course (Requires Admin Token)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "React Frontend Mastery",
    "description": "Learn React hooks, context, and routing.",
    "instructor": "John Doe",
    "price": 49,
    "category": "Web Development"
}

### 3. Get Single Course by ID (Replace with an actual ID from your database)
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/courses/65f123456789abcdef012345

### 4. Update a Course by ID (Requires Admin Token)
PUT http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/courses/65f123456789abcdef012345
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "price": 59
}

### 5. Delete a Course by ID (Requires Admin Token)
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/courses/65f123456789abcdef012345
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Create a Payment Order (Requires Auth Token)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/enrollments/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "courseId": "REPLACE_WITH_A_VALID_COURSE_ID_FROM_DB"
}

### 7. Get My Enrolled Courses (Requires Auth Token)
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/enrollments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}